        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{x+4}{(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+3x+2&=(x+1)(x+2)\\\\x^2+4x+3&=(x+1)(x+3)\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{x^2+3x+2}-\\frac{1}{x^2+4x+3}&=\\frac{2(x+3)}{(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)}-\\frac{x+2}{(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)}\\\\&=\\frac{2x+6-(x+2)}{(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)}\\\\&=\\frac{x+4}{(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)}\\end{align*}$$",
